WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.770
A café cuts the price of its sandwich.

2
00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:04.530
Nothing else changes.

3
00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:07.400
By lunchtime the queue is out of the door,

4
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.670
and the café sells far
more sandwiches than usual.

5
00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:12.670
The manager is delighted.

6
00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:15.000
Demand has gone up, she says.

7
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.190
An economist would say: not quite.

8
00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:21.100
So why do economists
insist that a price cut

9
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.410
does not increase demand?

10
00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:27.080
In this mission, you'll draw demand
curves from a demand schedule,

11
00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:28.800
and see what moves them.

12
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.270
Then you'll change prices and
other conditions in the graph lab,

13
00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:35.190
and predict what the curve does each time.

14
00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:39.240
Your mission: find out exactly
what a price cut changes,

15
00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.590
and what it leaves alone.
